00:50:22.180 --> 00:50:23.215 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: I'm not sure
it's hacking.

00:50:23.215 --> 00:50:25.080 align:middle line:84%
Like, PvP is the opposite
of [UNINTELLIGIBLE].

00:50:25.080 --> 00:50:26.606 align:middle line:90%
AUDIENCE: I mean it's not--

00:50:26.606 --> 00:50:28.240 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: I think it's
definitely player interaction

00:50:28.240 --> 00:50:30.220 align:middle line:90%
more than player action.

00:50:30.220 --> 00:50:32.040 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: Yeah, I believe
it's interaction.

00:50:32.040 --> 00:50:33.950 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: Something like having
PvP tournaments, I

00:50:33.950 --> 00:50:36.690 align:middle line:84%
think, would be definitely
a lot of interaction.

00:50:36.690 --> 00:50:37.100 align:middle line:90%
AUDIENCE: Yeah.

00:50:37.100 --> 00:50:40.570 align:middle line:84%
I think that's the distinction
between griefing and like

00:50:40.570 --> 00:50:42.075 align:middle line:90%
people fighting each other.

00:50:42.075 --> 00:50:43.740 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: Griefing can be
an [UNINTELLIGIBLE].

00:50:43.740 --> 00:50:47.550 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: What I got from this
article is that acting is

00:50:47.550 --> 00:50:50.013 align:middle line:84%
like, I go and kill someone
and ha, I killed

00:50:50.013 --> 00:50:50.620 align:middle line:90%
them and that's it.

00:50:50.620 --> 00:50:52.475 align:middle line:84%
Or I go through the world, it's
like, I killed a monster,

00:50:52.475 --> 00:50:53.190 align:middle line:90%
I killed a monster.

00:50:53.190 --> 00:50:54.260 align:middle line:90%
And you just have a goal.

00:50:54.260 --> 00:50:55.480 align:middle line:84%
If you want to get the
goal instead of

00:50:55.480 --> 00:50:58.210 align:middle line:90%
diverting from your goal.

00:50:58.210 --> 00:50:58.800 align:middle line:90%
So, I don't know.

00:50:58.800 --> 00:51:02.710 align:middle line:84%
I definitely think griefing
can be hugely interactive.

00:51:02.710 --> 00:51:04.491 align:middle line:84%
But there could be a
whole bunch of--

00:51:04.491 --> 00:51:08.210 align:middle line:84%
in EVE if you infiltrate
someone's company and you--

00:51:08.210 --> 00:51:10.310 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: Steal ten thousand
dollars' worth of their money.

00:51:10.310 --> 00:51:10.660 align:middle line:90%
AUDIENCE: Exactly.

00:51:10.660 --> 00:51:13.520 align:middle line:84%
That's hugely interactive
griefing.

00:51:13.520 --> 00:51:15.280 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: I don't think
that's griefing.

00:51:15.280 --> 00:51:16.500 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: Consider Team
Fortress, right.

00:51:16.500 --> 00:51:18.410 align:middle line:84%
There's Team Fortress
player interaction.

00:51:18.410 --> 00:51:21.910 align:middle line:84%
Because that means it's
a socializer game.

00:51:21.910 --> 00:51:24.020 align:middle line:84%
PROFESSOR: I personally do not
think Team Fortress falls

00:51:24.020 --> 00:51:27.850 align:middle line:84%
under player interacting
with team.

00:51:27.850 --> 00:51:29.240 align:middle line:90%
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

00:51:29.240 --> 00:51:32.121 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: But Left
for Dead is.

00:51:32.121 --> 00:51:35.050 align:middle line:90%
PROFESSOR: [UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:51:35.050 --> 00:51:35.940 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: There's definitely
interaction happening--

00:51:35.940 --> 00:51:36.340 align:middle line:90%
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

00:51:36.340 --> 00:51:38.482 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: I'd say probably
more-- it depends on what

00:51:38.482 --> 00:51:38.880 align:middle line:90%
you're doing

00:51:38.880 --> 00:51:41.600 align:middle line:90%
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

00:51:41.600 --> 00:51:43.170 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: So with Left for Dead
you can play-- you're

00:51:43.170 --> 00:51:46.160 align:middle line:84%
interacting, but then you're
also online and you can go

00:51:46.160 --> 00:51:48.840 align:middle line:84%
against other players
who are actually the

00:51:48.840 --> 00:51:50.983 align:middle line:90%
zombies, against you.

00:51:50.983 --> 00:51:51.406 align:middle line:90%
PROFESSOR: Right.

00:51:51.406 --> 00:51:55.370 align:middle line:84%
So let's talk about the basic
[UNINTELLIGIBLE].

00:51:55.370 --> 00:52:02.430 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: So the basic, most
common mode is going to be

00:52:02.430 --> 00:52:04.370 align:middle line:84%
four players playing
cooperatively

00:52:04.370 --> 00:52:07.440 align:middle line:90%
against the game world.

00:52:07.440 --> 00:52:09.860 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: That's just
interacting with the world.

00:52:09.860 --> 00:52:17.790 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: And there is a lot
of interaction that goes on

00:52:17.790 --> 00:52:20.808 align:middle line:84%
between players, because you
cannot basically survive

00:52:20.808 --> 00:52:22.640 align:middle line:84%
unless you get each
others' backs.

00:52:22.640 --> 00:52:24.080 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: So I would
say it's--

00:52:24.080 --> 00:52:26.440 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: And there's
built-in functions

00:52:26.440 --> 00:52:27.410 align:middle line:90%
to help other people.

00:52:27.410 --> 00:52:29.860 align:middle line:84%
So someone might get back up
on a ledge and he'll be

00:52:29.860 --> 00:52:31.130 align:middle line:84%
holding on and you have
to pull him back up.

00:52:31.130 --> 00:52:31.410 align:middle line:90%
AUDIENCE: Or smokers.

00:52:31.410 --> 00:52:34.730 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: At the same time,
there's also an intelligent

00:52:34.730 --> 00:52:38.830 align:middle line:84%
engine that plans that level
for you and places zombies

00:52:38.830 --> 00:52:43.490 align:middle line:84%
specifically to maintain you
in a state of nervousness.

00:52:43.490 --> 00:52:45.830 align:middle line:84%
And so it's different every
single time you play.

00:52:45.830 --> 00:52:49.230 align:middle line:84%
So those balance out and
probably place it somewhere in

00:52:49.230 --> 00:52:49.590 align:middle line:90%
the middle.

00:52:49.590 --> 00:52:52.501 align:middle line:84%
Maybe a little bit more player
biased than world biased,

00:52:52.501 --> 00:52:55.500 align:middle line:84%
because you really have
to stick together.

00:52:55.500 --> 00:52:58.250 align:middle line:84%
PROFESSOR: So, it's weird
because it's almost like, you

00:52:58.250 --> 00:52:59.870 align:middle line:90%
want to have like a plane.

00:52:59.870 --> 00:53:01.120 align:middle line:90%
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

00:53:01.120 --> 00:53:03.725 align:middle line:90%


00:53:03.725 --> 00:53:05.460 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: I think the big
problem with this sort of

00:53:05.460 --> 00:53:08.650 align:middle line:84%
graph is that you can't really
necessarily separate games

00:53:08.650 --> 00:53:11.570 align:middle line:90%
into one of these quadrants.

00:53:11.570 --> 00:53:12.820 align:middle line:90%
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

00:53:12.820 --> 00:53:15.146 align:middle line:90%


00:53:15.146 --> 00:53:16.760 align:middle line:84%
PROFESSOR: And that
is actually also--

00:53:16.760 --> 00:53:18.240 align:middle line:90%
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

00:53:18.240 --> 00:53:20.450 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: It might be a little
more useful to actually draw

00:53:20.450 --> 00:53:25.090 align:middle line:84%
areas within the graph to
represent a game, I guess.

00:53:25.090 --> 00:53:29.230 align:middle line:84%
Draw the area that encompasses
all the pieces the game

00:53:29.230 --> 00:53:30.490 align:middle line:90%
represents.

00:53:30.490 --> 00:53:31.740 align:middle line:90%
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

00:53:31.740 --> 00:53:34.756 align:middle line:90%


00:53:34.756 --> 00:53:39.560 align:middle line:84%
PROFESSOR: Like Halo co-op and
Halo multiplayer, and player

00:53:39.560 --> 00:53:40.810 align:middle line:90%
versus player.

00:53:40.810 --> 00:53:43.560 align:middle line:90%


00:53:43.560 --> 00:53:47.075 align:middle line:84%
That will probably be a little
refinement, if I create some

00:53:47.075 --> 00:53:50.160 align:middle line:84%
sort of scatter chart
or Venn diagram.

00:53:50.160 --> 00:53:51.540 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: Because I could
definitely see there being a

00:53:51.540 --> 00:53:54.450 align:middle line:84%
game where there's a lot of
acting on the world and

00:53:54.450 --> 00:53:55.760 align:middle line:90%
interacting with players.

00:53:55.760 --> 00:53:58.610 align:middle line:84%
And if you're just separating
these into distinct points,

00:53:58.610 --> 00:54:01.400 align:middle line:84%
that isn't possible
with this graph.

00:54:01.400 --> 00:54:03.810 align:middle line:84%
PROFESSOR: So that's another
problem, is the assumption

00:54:03.810 --> 00:54:08.980 align:middle line:84%
that acting and interacting
are--

00:54:08.980 --> 00:54:10.235 align:middle line:90%
AUDIENCE: Mutually exclusive?

00:54:10.235 --> 00:54:11.720 align:middle line:84%
PROFESSOR: They're mutually
opposite.

00:54:11.720 --> 00:54:12.970 align:middle line:90%
[UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:54:12.970 --> 00:54:16.670 align:middle line:90%


00:54:16.670 --> 00:54:18.318 align:middle line:84%
Do people generally
accept this?

00:54:18.318 --> 00:54:18.766 align:middle line:90%
AUDIENCE: No, no.

00:54:18.766 --> 00:54:20.900 align:middle line:84%
They do less acting
than interacting.

00:54:20.900 --> 00:54:23.610 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: If you just warp
space, then you can have

00:54:23.610 --> 00:54:24.000 align:middle line:90%
[UNINTELLIGIBLE].

00:54:24.000 --> 00:54:25.250 align:middle line:90%
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

00:54:25.250 --> 00:54:27.745 align:middle line:90%


00:54:27.745 --> 00:54:30.655 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: I think if you had
different values for player

00:54:30.655 --> 00:54:32.110 align:middle line:84%
world interacting
and acting would

00:54:32.110 --> 00:54:34.540 align:middle line:90%
necessarily be connected.

00:54:34.540 --> 00:54:38.661 align:middle line:84%
I think EVE definitely in world
is very high, and in

00:54:38.661 --> 00:54:40.736 align:middle line:90%
player is very high.

00:54:40.736 --> 00:54:43.050 align:middle line:84%
PROFESSOR: World very high,
player very high.

00:54:43.050 --> 00:54:45.740 align:middle line:84%
But I mean, player is
interacting and world is

00:54:45.740 --> 00:54:46.650 align:middle line:90%
acting on the world.

00:54:46.650 --> 00:54:48.820 align:middle line:90%
AUDIENCE: On the world still.

00:54:48.820 --> 00:54:49.870 align:middle line:90%
[UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:54:49.870 --> 00:54:52.210 align:middle line:90%
PROFESSOR: I mean, because--

00:54:52.210 --> 00:54:55.100 align:middle line:84%
you're exploring the world
spatially a lot.

00:54:55.100 --> 00:54:58.250 align:middle line:84%
Are you exploring the systems
of the world a lot?

00:54:58.250 --> 00:55:00.571 align:middle line:84%
Or are you really exploring the
systems set up by people?

00:55:00.571 --> 00:55:02.860 align:middle line:90%
AUDIENCE: That's true.

00:55:02.860 --> 00:55:07.930 align:middle line:84%
PROFESSOR: The nice thing about
things like EVE Online--

00:55:07.930 --> 00:55:08.660 align:middle line:90%
also [UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:55:08.660 --> 00:55:13.958 align:middle line:84%
EVE Online [UNINTELLIGIBLE]
game basically, where you

00:55:13.958 --> 00:55:15.260 align:middle line:90%
start off as a captain.

00:55:15.260 --> 00:55:16.700 align:middle line:84%
Correct me if I'm
wrong with this.

00:55:16.700 --> 00:55:19.354 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: It's a super-sandbox
game.

00:55:19.354 --> 00:55:22.198 align:middle line:84%
PROFESSOR: But for the
most part, you're

00:55:22.198 --> 00:55:24.094 align:middle line:90%
traveling in space.

00:55:24.094 --> 00:55:26.830 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: Can you get out of
your ship and walk on foot?

00:55:26.830 --> 00:55:27.470 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: Have they added that,
because I know they

00:55:27.470 --> 00:55:30.000 align:middle line:84%
wanted to add an expansion where
you could actually walk

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:31.140 align:middle line:90%
on planets.

00:55:31.140 --> 00:55:32.950 align:middle line:84%
Last time I heard,
they hadn't.

00:55:32.950 --> 00:55:34.220 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: Last I heard
they hadn't.

00:55:34.220 --> 00:55:37.370 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: Dust 66 or something
like that.

00:55:37.370 --> 00:55:37.895 align:middle line:84%
PROFESSOR:
[UNINTELLIGIBLE PHRASE]

00:55:37.895 --> 00:55:40.340 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: It's a
separate game.

00:55:40.340 --> 00:55:42.560 align:middle line:84%
PROFESSOR: No, you're traveling
through space.

00:55:42.560 --> 00:55:45.030 align:middle line:90%
[UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:55:45.030 --> 00:55:48.895 align:middle line:84%
But the whole idea is that it's
all built around this

00:55:48.895 --> 00:55:50.875 align:middle line:84%
economy, where [UNINTELLIGIBLE]
mining,

00:55:50.875 --> 00:55:52.990 align:middle line:90%
[UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:55:52.990 --> 00:55:53.285 align:middle line:90%
cash.

00:55:53.285 --> 00:55:57.110 align:middle line:84%
But the real power in the game
comes when players start to

00:55:57.110 --> 00:55:59.040 align:middle line:90%
ally with each other.

00:55:59.040 --> 00:56:01.980 align:middle line:84%
Form armadas, form
trade groups.

00:56:01.980 --> 00:56:06.880 align:middle line:84%
Form areas that you can
patrol and control.

00:56:06.880 --> 00:56:09.325 align:middle line:84%
And areas where you want to
agree that if you don't get

00:56:09.325 --> 00:56:13.689 align:middle line:84%
along with the people who are in
control of this space, you

00:56:13.689 --> 00:56:14.516 align:middle line:84%
will die when you
fly in there.

00:56:14.516 --> 00:56:18.484 align:middle line:84%
And the only thing that's making
that happen are other

00:56:18.484 --> 00:56:20.964 align:middle line:84%
players deciding that this
social contract is

00:56:20.964 --> 00:56:21.460 align:middle line:90%
[UNINTELLIGIBLE].

00:56:21.460 --> 00:56:24.436 align:middle line:90%
So it's pretty damn amazing.

00:56:24.436 --> 00:56:27.466 align:middle line:84%
What some folks were talking
about earlier was a big story

00:56:27.466 --> 00:56:30.680 align:middle line:84%
about how, basically, one person
got into a very, very

00:56:30.680 --> 00:56:33.755 align:middle line:84%
powerful position in
one of these clans.

00:56:33.755 --> 00:56:35.540 align:middle line:90%
And decided to defect.

00:56:35.540 --> 00:56:42.360 align:middle line:84%
Take a majority of one clan's
financial resources with him.

00:56:42.360 --> 00:56:46.090 align:middle line:84%
And-- remember, this is a
fairly modern massive

00:56:46.090 --> 00:56:47.330 align:middle line:90%
multiplayer online game.

00:56:47.330 --> 00:56:50.370 align:middle line:84%
In-game assets can now be
traded for real money.

00:56:50.370 --> 00:56:51.350 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: It's illegal
so that--

00:56:51.350 --> 00:56:52.000 align:middle line:90%
PROFESSOR: It's illegal.

00:56:52.000 --> 00:56:52.880 align:middle line:90%
AUDIENCE: Like, in-game.

00:56:52.880 --> 00:56:55.430 align:middle line:84%
So you can get your
account banned.

00:56:55.430 --> 00:56:59.000 align:middle line:84%
So what happened, if I'm talking
about the one that

00:56:59.000 --> 00:57:00.150 align:middle line:90%
you're talking about.

00:57:00.150 --> 00:57:03.080 align:middle line:84%
Someone got to a really
powerful place in

00:57:03.080 --> 00:57:04.110 align:middle line:90%
this banking clan.

00:57:04.110 --> 00:57:06.400 align:middle line:84%
And then took all of
their assets and

00:57:06.400 --> 00:57:07.510 align:middle line:90%
traded it for real money.

00:57:07.510 --> 00:57:11.130 align:middle line:84%
So he got $10,000 by
selling it off.

00:57:11.130 --> 00:57:13.070 align:middle line:90%
AUDIENCE: [UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:57:13.070 --> 00:57:16.326 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: One was a guy who
infiltrated the clan

00:57:16.326 --> 00:57:17.763 align:middle line:84%
[UNINTELLIGIBLE] that
much money.

00:57:17.763 --> 00:57:20.300 align:middle line:84%
One was like a parent who was
going into financial trouble

00:57:20.300 --> 00:57:24.285 align:middle line:84%
and held a fifth of the assets
of the major bank, and cashed

00:57:24.285 --> 00:57:28.575 align:middle line:84%
it in for $6,000 to help pay off
part of his house and his

00:57:28.575 --> 00:57:29.988 align:middle line:90%
kids' medical bills.

00:57:29.988 --> 00:57:32.350 align:middle line:84%
And then posted an apology on
the board and quit the game.

00:57:32.350 --> 00:57:34.360 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: I thought he got
banned from the game.

00:57:34.360 --> 00:57:35.620 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: He was banned
from the game, but he

00:57:35.620 --> 00:57:38.494 align:middle line:90%
also quit the game.

00:57:38.494 --> 00:57:40.949 align:middle line:90%
AUDIENCE: [UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:57:40.949 --> 00:57:42.225 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: He was like, I'm
sorry, everybody, but this is

00:57:42.225 --> 00:57:44.295 align:middle line:90%
kind of important.

00:57:44.295 --> 00:57:46.510 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: The amazing one
was the guy who actually

00:57:46.510 --> 00:57:51.170 align:middle line:84%
infiltrated the company and
just took it down as a

00:57:51.170 --> 00:57:52.720 align:middle line:90%
years-long operation--

00:57:52.720 --> 00:57:53.328 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: [UNINTELLIGIBLE]
thought he was a

00:57:53.328 --> 00:57:54.070 align:middle line:90%
friend and all that.

00:57:54.070 --> 00:57:55.550 align:middle line:90%
AUDIENCE: Yeah.

00:57:55.550 --> 00:57:57.870 align:middle line:84%
Trying to get in and then
managed to take down this

00:57:57.870 --> 00:58:00.060 align:middle line:90%
gigantic in-game corporation.

00:58:00.060 --> 00:58:01.318 align:middle line:84%
AUDIENCE: How many active
players are

00:58:01.318 --> 00:58:02.892 align:middle line:90%
there on EVE Online?

00:58:02.892 --> 00:58:04.620 align:middle line:90%
A hundred thousand?

00:58:04.620 --> 00:58:04.846 align:middle line:90%
AUDIENCE: No.

00:58:04.846 --> 00:58:07.400 align:middle line:84%
I feel like the active
players are--

00:58:07.400 --> 00:58:07.990 align:middle line:90%
PROFESSOR: [UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:58:07.990 --> 00:58:11.230 align:middle line:90%
AUDIENCE: At any moment?

00:58:11.230 --> 00:58:14.960 align:middle line:84%
PROFESSOR: No, I mean active
current players who have

00:58:14.960 --> 00:58:16.720 align:middle line:90%
